Based on the post‐vaccination effective reproduction number (~1.22) and 327 infections at day 20, the outbreak will grow slowly over the next 20 days.  Approximating with an SIR model (β=0.18, γ=0.1) and stochastic variability (~15% CV) yields roughly 850 new infections (median) between days 21–40, with a distribution roughly Normal.  

