By day 20, about 1,006 people remain susceptible. The day-21 campaign should vaccinate roughly a quarter of them (~250), leaving ~750 unvaccinated susceptible people. Since there are still 3,389 infectious people, most unvaccinated susceptibles should be infected, but the epidemic is already overshooting the herd-immunity point and many current infections will recover over the next ~10 days. Vaccinated susceptibles have only about 5% of the usual per-exposure risk, so most of them should escape infection.

My forecast is therefore centered around roughly 690 new infections, with uncertainty mainly from stochastic transmission, vaccination allocation among remaining susceptibles, and recovery/infection-age details.

