By day 20, Riverton still has a very large infectious pool: 911 infectious out of 5,000. The day-21 vaccination campaign should cut the effective susceptible pool substantially, but not enough to immediately make transmission subcritical: about 3,871 people remain never-infected, and roughly 25% of them will be vaccinated, leaving an “effective susceptible” pool around 2,950 after accounting for 95% protection.

Using the recent incidence and the 10-day infectious period, I’d expect infections to keep rising for roughly another week, peak, then decline as susceptible depletion and vaccination dominate. A deterministic approximation gives around 2,200 additional infections by day 60, with stochastic variation of a few hundred people.

