At day 20, only about 1,006 people remain susceptible, while infectious prevalence is extremely high. A day-21 vaccination campaign covering 25% of the population likely protects only about 250 of those remaining susceptibles, and with 95% efficacy those vaccinated people still have a small breakthrough risk. Most unvaccinated susceptibles should be infected before transmission dies out, while only a minority of vaccinated susceptibles become infected.

My forecast is therefore centered around roughly 690 additional infections by day 40, with moderate stochastic spread.  
